# Read Design Code Clauses

---

## Trigger

Use this skill whenever a calculation, memo, note or answer needs a code provision:
- "What does AASHTO say about orthotropic deck fatigue?"
- "What load factor applies to counterweight dead load in the Movable spec?"
- "Find BDP guidance on strengthening steel girders"
- Any time a clause number, table value, resistance factor or equation is about to be written down.

CALCULATION_RULES §1: **never supply a code value from memory.** This skill is how you read it.

---

## Codes available and precedence (EOR decision 2026-09-07)

| Prec. | Key | Document | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `ca` | California Amendments to AASHTO LRFD BDS 8th Ed. (Sept 2025 compilation) | Binding. Bookmarked by section and article. Replaces/adds to specific AASHTO articles; if an article is in `ca`, that text governs. |
| 1 | `bdp` | Caltrans Bridge Design Practice, 5th Ed. | 21 chapter PDFs; needs `--chapter`. Guidance and worked examples conforming to AASHTO 8th + Amendments. |
| 2 | `movable` | AASHTO LRFD Movable Highway Bridge Design Specs, 3rd Ed. 2023 | No bookmarks; search text. Section TOC precedes each section body. |
| 3 | `lrfd` | AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specs, 8th Ed. 2017 | Bookmarks to article level (coarser in some sections); text search as fallback. |
| 4 | `aisc` | AISC Steel Construction Manual, 15th Ed. 2017 | Bookmarks at Part/Chapter level; Specification starts PDF p 1389, Commentary p 1697. |

None of the PDFs carry page labels; the printed page number (e.g. `6-45`, `3-29B`) is in the page text. Chapter and section map: `01_References/Design Codes/CODES_INDEX.md`.

---

## Step-by-Step Procedure

### Step 1 — Locate (always check `ca` first for an AASHTO article)

```bash
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py ca --clause 3.4.1
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py lrfd --clause 3.4.1
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py movable --search "counterweight" --max 30
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py bdp --chapter 16.1 --toc "cover plate"
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py aisc --toc "Table J3.2"
```

`--clause` checks bookmarks first, then text with a line-start match, so `6.6.1` does not hit `6.6.1.2`. The first text hits are usually the section TOC entries; the body page follows.

### Step 2 — Read the page

```bash
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py ca --pdf-page 41 --chars 6000
.venv/Scripts/python tools/read-code/find_clause.py lrfd --pdf-page 700 --chars 6000
```

Read the provision **and its commentary** (AASHTO prints commentary in the right column; extraction interleaves them — look for the `C3.4.1` prefix). Read the neighbouring page if the clause runs over. In `ca`, amended text is what Caltrans requires; the page header shows the section and printed page (`3-29B` style pages are Caltrans insertions).

### Step 3 — Cite

Format: `<Document short name> <Ed.> Art. <number> (p. <printed>; PDF p <n>)`.

- `CA Amendments (Sept 2025) Art. 3.4.1, Table 3.4.1-1 (p. 3-13; PDF p 41)`
- `AASHTO LRFD 8th Art. 6.6.1.2.3, Table 6.6.1.2.3-1 (p. 6-xx; PDF p nnn)` — add `not amended by CA` or `as amended, see CA p …`.
- `AASHTO Movable 3rd Art. 2.4.1.2 (p. 2-7; PDF p 41)`
- `Caltrans BDP 5th Ch 6.2 §6.2.5 (p. 6.2-11; PDF p 11)`
- `AISC 15th Spec. Sec. J3.6 (PDF p 1573)`

In a calc script the citation goes in the trailing comment of the value (CALCULATION_RULES §1).

### Step 4 — Precedence check

If the provision exists in more than one document, look it up in every applicable one, apply the highest precedence, and record the others' values and the difference in the calc's `ASSUMPTIONS`/notes. Do not resolve a conflict yourself; flag it (CALCULATION_RULES §8).

---

## Rules

1. Quote only what the page text shows. Extraction can scramble equations and tables; when a table or equation is needed, render the page and view it: `render_pages.py --pdf "<code pdf>" --pages <n> --dpi 200` (the read-asbuilt renderer works on any PDF), then Read the PNG.
2. An AASHTO LRFD article is never cited without first checking whether `ca` amends it.
3. Never cite an edition other than those in the table above.
4. Caltrans STPs, Caltrans Std Specs 2025 / SSPs 2025 and AWS D1.5 are **not** in the references. If a question needs them, say so and stop; do not substitute memory.
5. Do not write into `01_References/Design Codes/` except `CODES_INDEX.md`.

